  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>signups-child - the child: loads each batch of sign-ups that keep the
contract into kafka_warehouse.user_events, and publishes every one that
breaks it to pdi-signups-rejects, unchanged, with the reason as its key.

1. Get records from stream: key, message, topic, partition, offset, timestamp.
2. JSON input: error handling on - a message whose registertime is not a
   number goes to Name the fault, which names the field. (A line that is not
   JSON reads as all nulls, so the contract check catches it.)
3. Check the contract (Data Validator): userid present; gender one of
   FEMALE, MALE, OTHER. Every rule is checked and the reasons joined.
4. Select values, Formula, Table output: as in the Use Cases lab.
5. Bad JSON and Broken contract: keep message and the reason, in the same
   order, so both feed one step. Publish reject: Kafka producer to
   pdi-signups-rejects, key reject_reason, message message.</note>
      <xloc>32</xloc>
      <yloc>32</yloc>
      <width>460</width>
      <heigth>260</heigth>
      <fontname>Segoe UI</fontname>
      <fontsize>10</fontsize>
      <fontbold>N</fontbold>
      <fontitalic>N</fontitalic>
